WEBVTT

00:00:00.812 --> 00:00:06.494
Long, long ago, at the very beginning of time.

00:00:06.554 --> 00:00:10.100
When everything was just getting sorted out, 

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:20.196
Stickly-Prickly Hedgehog lived on the banks of the Turbid Amazon, eating shelly snails and things.

00:00:20.255 --> 00:00:28.796
He had a friend, Slow-and-Solid Tortoise, who ate mostly green lettuces.

00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:36.240
There was also a Painted Jaguar living on the banks of the Turbid Amazon.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.599
He ate everything that he could catch.

00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:47.898
When he could not catch deer or monkeys, he caught frogs and beetles.

00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:50.920
How to catch frogs and beetles?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.002
Jump on frogs before they jump on you.

00:00:55.062 --> 00:01:00.415
Pin your beetles down with a sharp claw.

00:01:00.474 --> 00:01:08.822
Live frogs can be a bit jumpy once they get into your insides.

00:01:08.882 --> 00:01:12.900
When he could not catch frogs and beetles, 

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:22.632
he went to his mother, Jaguar, who told him how to eat hedgehogs and tortoises.

00:01:22.691 --> 00:01:29.000
My son, she said, when you find a hedgehog, 

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:35.504
you must drop him into the water, then he will uncoil.

00:01:35.564 --> 00:01:44.489
When you catch a tortoise, you must scoop him out of his shell with your paw.

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:50.600
One beautiful night on the banks of the Turbid Amazon, 

00:01:50.660 --> 00:02:01.152
Painted Jaguar found Stickly-Prickly Hedgehog and Slow-and-Solid Tortoise sitting behind a clump of bushes.

00:02:01.212 --> 00:02:08.421
Stickly prickly curled himself up into a ball because he was a hedgehog.

00:02:08.481 --> 00:02:16.549
Slow-and-Solid pulled his head and feet into his shell because he was a tortoise.

00:02:16.609 --> 00:02:21.340
Now listen to me, said Painted Jaguar, 

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.600
because this is very important. 

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:35.712
My mother said that when I meet a hedgehog, I have to drop him into the water, and then he will uncoil.

00:02:35.772 --> 00:02:43.126
And when I meet a tortoise, I am to scoop him out of his shell with my paw.

00:02:43.186 --> 00:02:49.210
So, which of you is hedgehog and which is tortoise?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:54.562
Because to save my spots, I can't tell.

00:02:54.622 --> 00:02:58.594
Are you sure what your mother said?

00:02:58.654 --> 00:03:00.494
said Stickly-Prickly.

00:03:00.554 --> 00:03:03.936
Are you quite sure?

00:03:03.996 --> 00:03:12.609
Perhaps she said that when you uncoil a tortoise, you must shell him out of the water with a scoop.

00:03:12.668 --> 00:03:19.971
I don't think it was that, said Painted Jaguar, feeling a little puzzled.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:24.521
Say it again slowly.

00:03:24.581 --> 00:03:37.746
Perhaps your mother said that when you water a hedgehog, you must drop him into your paw, said Slow-and-Solid.

00:03:37.806 --> 00:03:48.142
You're making my spots ache, said Painted Jaguar, and besides, I didn't ask you for advice.

00:03:48.202 --> 00:03:54.899
I only want to know which of you is hedgehog and which is tortoise.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:04:04.291
I shan't tell you, said Stickly-Prickly, but you can scoop me out with my shell if you like.

00:04:04.351 --> 00:04:07.814
Ah-ha!

00:04:07.874 --> 00:04:09.536
Said Painted Jaguar.

00:04:09.596 --> 00:04:14.219
Now I know you're tortoise!

00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:21.600
Painted Jaguar darted out his paddy-paw just as Stickly-Prickly curled himself up,

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:35.062
and of course Jaguar's paddy-paw was filled with prickles. Worse than that, he knocked Stickly-Prickly away into the bushes.

00:04:35.121 --> 00:04:43.269
Painted Jaguar put his paddy-paw into his mouth, and of course the prickles hurt him worse than ever.

00:04:43.329 --> 00:04:50.885
As soon as he could speak, he said, If he isn't tortoise, then who are you?

00:04:50.905 --> 00:04:55.148
I am Tortoise,

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:57.068
Said Slow-and-Solid.

00:04:57.128 --> 00:04:59.470
Your mother was quite right.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:06.054
She said that you were to scoop me out of my shell with your paw.

00:05:06.114 --> 00:05:10.442
You didn't say she said that a minute ago.

00:05:10.502 --> 00:05:12.287
Said Painted Jaguar.

00:05:12.347 --> 00:05:14.926
Sucking his paddy-paw.

00:05:14.986 --> 00:05:23.237
Well, suppose you say that I said that she said something quite different, said Tortoise.

00:05:23.296 --> 00:05:32.484
It doesn't matter, because if she said what you said I said she said, it's just the same as if I said what she said she said.

00:05:32.544 --> 00:05:39.312
So if you want to see me swim away, you should drop me in the water.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:45.905
I don't believe you, said Painted Jaguar.

00:05:45.964 --> 00:05:51.644
I don't think you want to be dropped in the water at all.

00:05:51.703 --> 00:05:52.756
Go on then.

00:05:52.816 --> 00:05:55.570
Jump in and be quick about it.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:06:03.260
Before Jaguar could change his mind, Slow-and-Solid quietly dived into the Turbid Amazon, 

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:11.294
swam underwater for a long way, and came out on the bank where Stickly-Prickly was waiting for him.

00:06:11.354 --> 00:06:20.522
The Turbid Amazon. The Turbid Amazon is quite like soup, a living soup.

00:06:20.582 --> 00:06:24.900
In the thick brown water that flows lazily down to the sea, 

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:45.176
you will find millions of eels, leeches, piranhas, snails, water beetles, weeds, nameless, disgusting things.

00:06:45.236 --> 00:06:59.076
Painted Jaguar howled up and down among the trees and the bushes by the side of the Turbid Amazon till his mother came.

00:06:59.136 --> 00:07:06.158
Son, son, said his mother, graciously waving her tail.

00:07:06.218 --> 00:07:13.260
What have you been doing that you shouldn't have done?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:16.553
Graciously waving tails.

00:07:16.613 --> 00:07:20.768
If you've got a tail, use it.

00:07:20.828 --> 00:07:31.664
Flick it at the end, ripple it down the middle, curl it slowly, and languorously.

00:07:31.724 --> 00:07:41.494
I scooped something out of its shell, and my paw is full of prickles, said Painted Jaguar.

00:07:41.554 --> 00:07:46.502
Son, son, said his mother.

00:07:46.562 --> 00:07:50.043
That was a hedgehog.

00:07:50.103 --> 00:07:55.360
You should drop hedgehogs into the water.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:58.557
I did that to the other thing.

00:07:58.617 --> 00:08:03.762
He said he was a tortoise and I didn't believe him.

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:08.456
Oh, let's go and live somewhere else.

00:08:08.516 --> 00:08:14.885
They are too clever on the turbid Amazon for poor me.

00:08:14.945 --> 00:08:23.525
Son, son, said his mother, listen and remember.

00:08:23.585 --> 00:08:35.503
A hedgehog curls up into a ball, and his prickles stick out every which way at once.

00:08:35.563 --> 00:08:40.157
A tortoise can't curl himself up,

00:08:40.216 --> 00:08:45.826
Mother Jaguar went on, still graciously waving her tail.

00:08:45.887 --> 00:08:53.872
He can only pull his head and legs into his shell.

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:59.954
Stickly-Prickly and Slow-and-Solid were listening in the bushes.

00:09:00.014 --> 00:09:06.776
I don't like Mother Jaguar one little bit, whispered Stickly-Prickly.

00:09:06.836 --> 00:09:12.250
Even Painted Jaguar can't forget those directions.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:15.742
It's a pity I can't swim.

00:09:15.802 --> 00:09:22.533
And it's a pity I can't curl up, said Slow-and-Solid.

00:09:22.593 --> 00:09:27.840
Painted Jaguar sat on the banks of the Turbid Amazon, 

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:36.556
sucking prickles out of his paw and saying to himself, Can't curl, but can swim.

00:09:36.616 --> 00:09:40.699
Slow, solid, that's him.

00:09:40.759 --> 00:09:44.331
Curls up, but can't swim.

00:09:44.391 --> 00:09:48.334
Stickly-Prickly, that's him.

00:09:48.394 --> 00:09:55.128
He'll never forget that in a month of Sundays, said Stickly-Prickly.

00:09:55.188 --> 00:09:58.169
Hold up my chin, Slow-and-Solid.

00:09:58.229 --> 00:09:59.889
I'm going to learn to swim.

00:09:59.909 --> 00:10:11.508
Oh, excellent, said Slow-and-Solid, holding up Stickly-Prickly's chin while he splashed in the waters of the Turbid Amazon.

00:10:11.568 --> 00:10:15.686
You'll make a fine swimmer yet, he said.

00:10:15.706 --> 00:10:25.343
Now, if you can unlace my back plates a little, I'll see if I can do some curling up.

00:10:25.403 --> 00:10:39.760
Stickly-Prickly unlaced Tortoise's back plates so that, by twisting and straining, Slow-and-Solid actually managed to curl up a bit.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:46.602
Then Stickly-Prickly practised swimming side-stroke, and Slow-and-Solid

00:10:46.662 --> 00:10:51.947
unlaced more of his plates and did some bending.

00:10:52.007 --> 00:10:55.406
Swimming and bending.

00:10:55.466 --> 00:11:00.443
When swimming, it is best to hold your breath and not breathe in.

00:11:00.503 --> 00:11:04.024
You can breathe out in small bubbles.

00:11:04.084 --> 00:11:12.426
When bending, it is better to breathe out in one great puff.

00:11:12.486 --> 00:11:20.450
Don't grunt quite so much, said Stickly-Prickly, or Painted Jaguar might hear us.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:26.160
Then Stickly-Prickly dived underwater and practised holding his breath, 

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:33.191
and Slow-and-Solid practised putting his hind legs behind his ears.

00:11:33.251 --> 00:11:43.934
Excellent, said Stickly-Prickly, but your back plates are all overlapping now, instead of lying side by side.

00:11:43.994 --> 00:11:55.246
Well, said Slow-and-Solid, your prickles have melted into one another, and you're growing to look a bit like a pine cone.

00:11:55.306 --> 00:11:56.728
Am I?

00:11:56.788 --> 00:11:58.660
Said Stickly-Prickly.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:01.682
That comes from soaking in the water.

00:12:01.742 --> 00:12:07.582
Oh, won't Painted Jaguar be surprised.

00:12:07.642 --> 00:12:18.500
The next day, Stickly-Prickly and Tortoise looked so different, they were almost the same.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.405
Painted Jaguar was astonished when he saw them.

00:12:23.465 --> 00:12:31.264
He fell backwards three times without stopping over his own painted tail.

00:12:31.324 --> 00:12:39.378
Good morning, said Stickly-Prickly, and how is your dear gracious Mummy today?

00:12:39.398 --> 00:12:44.420
Well, she's quite well, thank you.

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:50.797
said Painted Jaguar, but you must forgive me if I don't recall your names.

00:12:50.857 --> 00:12:56.375
Don't you remember what your mother told you? said Stickly-Prickly.

00:12:56.435 --> 00:12:59.237
Can't curl, but can swim.

00:12:59.297 --> 00:13:01.779
Slow, solid, that's him.

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:04.901
Curls up, but can't swim.

00:13:04.961 --> 00:13:08.002
Stickly-Prickly, that's him.

00:13:08.062 --> 00:13:19.596
Then they both curled themselves up and rolled round and round Painted Jaguar till his eyes turned cartwheels in his head.

00:13:19.656 --> 00:13:23.254
He ran wailing to his mother.

00:13:23.314 --> 00:13:25.706
Oh mother!

00:13:25.766 --> 00:13:29.660
He said, There are two new animals in the woods today, 

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:36.306
and the one that you said could swim swims, and the one that you said couldn't curl up

00:13:36.366 --> 00:13:43.988
curls! They've gone shares in their prickles, because both of them are scaly all over.

00:13:44.048 --> 00:13:51.950
Son, son, said Mother Jaguar, graciously waving her tail.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:59.409
A hedgehog is a hedgehog, and a tortoise is a tortoise.

00:13:59.469 --> 00:14:03.875
They could never be anything else.

00:14:03.935 --> 00:14:16.692
But it isn't a hedgehog, and it isn't a tortoise, it's a little bit of both, and I don't know its proper name.

00:14:16.712 --> 00:14:22.964
Oh nonsense, said Mother Jaguar.

00:14:23.024 --> 00:14:28.452
Everything has a proper name. I should call it

00:14:28.512 --> 00:14:33.346
Armadillo, and leave well alone.

00:14:33.406 --> 00:14:53.041
So Painted Jaguar did just as he was told, and from that day to this no one on the banks of the Turbid Amazon has ever called Stickly-Prickly or Slow-and-Solid anything except Armadillo.

00:14:53.101 --> 00:14:57.900
There are hedgehogs and tortoises in other places, of course, 

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:05.700
but the real old and clever kind, with their scales lying lippity-lappity like pine cones, 

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:17.653
that live on the banks of the Turbid Amazon, are still called armadillos, because they are so clever.